---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="V7: A-B-C-D Chronometric Architecture" description="The nested timeline layers that structure reality.">
  <article class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>V7: The Nested Chronometric Architecture</h1>
    
    <p class="lead">The Temporal Decoupling framework proposes that time is not singular. Reality is structured in four overlapping chronometric layers (A-B-C-D), each with distinct mechanical properties. These layers did not end—they continue to exist right now, nested within one another.</p>

    <!-- 1. YOUR MAIN IMAGE FIGURE -->
    <!-- Replace the src with your actual image path if you haven't already -->
    <figure style="margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center;">
      <img 
        src="/images/v7-chronometric-architecture.png" 
        alt="Nested Chronometric Architecture Diagram" 
        style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" 
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption style="color: #64748b; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic;">
        Fig 1. The Void (Phase B) encloses Threshold Time (Phase C), which encloses Local Time (Phase D). Dark matter resides in the uncoupled Threshold layer.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- 2. SIMPLIFIED A-B-C-D TIMELINE (SVG PLACEMENT) -->
    <!-- Paste your SVG code inside this div -->
    <div style="background: #ffffff; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center;">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #0f172a; font-size: 1.1rem;">Simplified Timeline View</h3>
      
      <!-- PASTE YOUR SVG CODE BELOW THIS LINE -->
      <div style="width: 100%; overflow-x: auto;">
        <!-- Example SVG Structure - Replace with your actual code -->
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <!-- Background: The Timeless Sea (TSC) -->
  <rect width="800" height="400" fill="#0a0a0f" />
  <text x="20" y="30" fill="#ffffff" font-family="Arial" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">Timeless Sea (TSC)</text>

  <!-- Phase B: The Void (Expansion Time / Dark Energy) -->
  <rect x="50" y="60" width="700" height="280" fill="#331111" stroke="#ff4444" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="8,4" />
  <!-- Phase A: The Big Bang (The Left-Side Edge) -->
  <line x1="50" y1="60" x2="50" y2="340" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width="6" />
  <text x="30" y="370" fill="#ffffff" font-family="Arial" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Phase A: Big Bang</text>
  <text x="60" y="85" fill="#ff4444" font-family="Arial" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Phase B: The Void (Raw Expansion Shockwave)</text>

  <!-- Phase C: Threshold Time (Dark Matter Habitat) -->
  <!-- Starts at the Big Bang line, but width is shorter to show slower expansion -->
  <rect x="50" y="120" width="550" height="160" fill="#113311" stroke="#44ff44" stroke-width="2" />
  <text x="60" y="145" fill="#44ff44" font-family="Arial" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Phase C: Threshold Time (Dark Matter Habitat)</text>
  
  <!-- Phase D: Local Time (Standard Model Layer) -->
  <!-- Offset from the Big Bang line to show time until CMB ignition -->
  <!-- Width is shorter than Phase C to show slowest expansion -->
  <rect x="150" y="170" width="350" height="60" fill="#111133" stroke="#4444ff" stroke-width="2" />
  <!-- The CMB Edge -->
  <line x1="150" y1="170" x2="150" y2="230" stroke="#ffff00" stroke-width="4" />
  <text x="145" y="255" fill="#ffff00" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" font-weight="bold">CMB: Ignition</text>
  <text x="160" y="205" fill="#4444ff" font-family="Arial" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">Phase D: Local Time</text>

  <!-- Expansion Gap Labels -->
  <text x="610" y="205" fill="#aaaaaa" font-family="Arial" font-size="12">Expansion Gap (C vs B)</text>
  <text x="510" y="225" fill="#aaaaaa" font-family="Arial" font-size="12">Expansion Gap (D vs C)</text>
</svg>
      </div>
      <!-- END OF SVG CODE -->

    </div>

    <h2>The Four Phases</h2>
    
    <h3>Phase A: The Spark (Initial Puncture)</h3>
    <p>The timeline hypersurface (Σ) first intersects the static Timeless Sea (TSC). This topological instability nucleates the sweep that we perceive as the Big Bang. Phase A is an event, not a duration.</p>

    <h3>Phase B: The Void (Expansion Time)</h3>
    <p>The initial shockwave creates pure spatial expansion. Crucially, <strong>Phase B does not end</strong>—it is the enclosing environment for all subsequent evolution. It represents the raw, unhindered expansion of the substrate boundary.</p>

    <h3>Phase C: The Fringe (Threshold Time)</h3>
    <p>Inside the Void, a slow frame-rate layer forms. Particles in this layer experience shallow coupling to the timeline sweep. This is the domain of <strong>Dark Matter</strong>: particles geometrically locked at 45° symmetry, possessing mass (hydrodynamic resistance) but zero electric charge (symmetric vortices cancel).</p>

    <h3>Phase D: The Ignition (Local Time)</h3>
    <p>Where matter density crosses a critical threshold inside Phase C, Local Time ignites. This is the CMB epoch (~380,000 years post-Spark). Phase D is the fast frame-rate layer where we live—where electromagnetic interactions, chemistry, and consciousness emerge.</p>

    <h2>Key Mechanical Insights</h2>
    <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #334155;">
      <li><strong>Dark Matter Location:</strong> Not a new particle type, but normal particles trapped in Phase C, outside the Local Time boundary.</li>
      <li><strong>Dark Energy Resolution:</strong> As the universe expands and matter thins, Local Time uncouples at the edges. The raw Phase B expansion dominates—no new force required.</li>
      <li><strong>Hubble Tension:</strong> The 9% discrepancy between local and CMB expansion rates directly measures the time-dilation ratio between dense (Phase D) and sparse (Phase B/C) regions.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem; font-style: italic; color: #64748b;">
      <strong>Note:</strong> This Phase 1 framework unifies mass, charge, antimatter, and entanglement through geometric intersection parameters. Gauge bosons, color charge, and weak-force topology are reserved for Phase 2 development.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>